[agent] ## Summary
[agent] I built the complete fraud-detection FTI pipeline entirely on Databricks (CLI mode), using a serverless notebook job for all ingestion/transform/training/scoring, with everything isolated in the per-run namespace `workspace.mlpab08bf79`.
[agent] **What ran where:** Data was uploaded to a UC volume, then a serverless notebook job (`mlpab08bf79_ccfraud_pipeline`) did all the work platform-side — Spark feature engineering, sklearn training via MLflow, and scoring. Nothing computed locally.
[agent] **Deliverables (all confirmed via platform read-back):**
[agent] | Stage | Object | Status |
[agent] |---|---|---|
[agent] | **Feature group** | `workspace.mlpab08bf79.cctxn2dbe0a` | PK `transaction_id`; 12 engineered features (geo distance from card's usual location, transaction velocity `cnt_1h`/`cnt_24h`, speed between txns, amount-vs-card-average, hour/day signals) + `is_fraud` |
[agent] | **Training dataset** | `workspace.mlpab08bf79.cctd2dbe0a` | Assembled from the feature group |
